{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/771763-damaging-demons","id":771763,"title":"Damaging Demons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-22T15:26:33-08:00","id":771763,"title":"Damaging Demons","content":"Consider the following situation: A Demon is using the Materialize Numem (As described in Inferno's Handbook), which allows to move from the Twilight aspect to material. How do you consider about causing damage in that creature considering this situation? The rule says, when the Corpus reach to 0, the demon is drag to hell. Ok, Corpus 0 means that you cause Aggravated damage enough to fulfill its Corpse. But in Material form, Lethal sources (like firing a gun, attacking with a blade) that you use to attack the demon, is it ALWAYS Lethal damage? Or when the Demon's Corpses fulfill with this mundane damage, is it converted to Aggravated, as happens with regular combat in NWOD System? How do you solve this in your game?<br /> <br /> The same question can be applied envolving another Ephemeral creatures in game, like ghost or spirits. Can be destroyed using only lethal damage source?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9723-winchester","name":"winchester","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T16:19:10-08:00","id":771824,"title":"","content":"Minor assumption: using god machine rules<br /> <br /> What you need is to research what it's bane is to deal lethal. Knowing it's bans will also greatly assist you in dealing with the demon.<br /> <br /> After it manifests I'd also suggest keeping it distracted as others draw a salt circle to cage it. I belive all ephemeral beings can't cross a line of salt in wod. For more in depth I'd suggest looking into the mortal interaction section in the ephemeral chapter in the god machine chronicle.<br /> <br /> Edit: I was wrong, lethal in twilight and aggrivated while manifested from their bane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2909,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","user":"Mr.F.I.X.","date":". 11-22-2015, 07:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T18:24:36-08:00","id":771957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/771763-damaging-demons?p=771824#post771824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Minor assumption: using god machine rules<br /> <br /> What you need is to research what it's bane is to deal lethal. Knowing it's bans will also greatly assist you in dealing with the demon.<br /> <br /> After it manifests I'd also suggest keeping it distracted as others draw a salt circle to cage it. I belive all ephemeral beings can't cross a line of salt in wod. For more in depth I'd suggest looking into the mortal interaction section in the ephemeral chapter in the god machine chronicle.<br /> <br /> Edit: I was wrong, lethal in twilight and aggrivated while manifested from their bane.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Fine! Now i saw in God Machine, and there says:<br /> <br /> &quot;Physical attacks on a manifest entity that normally cause<br /> lethal damage only cause bashing damage unless the attack<br /> utilizes the entity\u2019s bane. Despite appearing to the naked eye<br /> and being solid, a manifest spirit, ghost, or angel doesn\u2019t have<br /> any internal organs to injure.&quot;<br /> <br /> My question is: when this bashing damage, caused by normal weapons, fills all the Corpus boxes, this &quot;normal weapon&quot; starts to cause Lethal, like happens in general combat? For example, the Spirit manifested (ghost, demon, whatever), have 7 Corpus. So the attacker have a Glock pistol in his hand and with the shots, have 7 sucess on attack roll. So the damage caused is 7 bashing damage, that i mark on Corpus boxes. If the hunter strikes again with the same gun, the damage counts as Lethal (because all the Corpus boxes was already filled with Bashing, like in normal combat rules) or the damage isn't counted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9723-winchester","name":"winchester","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T19:56:57-08:00","id":772020,"title":"","content":"Yes once the damage boxes are filled they with bashing each further bashing will cause one of the previous to convert to lethal. General rule without any specific rule saying otherwise here.<br /> <br /> The only specific rule to note here is ephemeral beings don't suffer from wound penalties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T04:04:59-08:00","id":772214,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, ok. The detail is that entity can &quot;dematerializes&quot; at any time, returning to its ephemeral and intangible form (against normal damage), right? So it can recover from the bashing damage in a few minutes to recover from bashing damage (15 minute each point to recover) and materialize again, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9723-winchester","name":"winchester","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T20:47:59-08:00","id":772769,"title":"","content":"Yes, if you want to get rid of it for longer, you'll need to destroy it's fetter, trap it with a ward, or abjure it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}